<% content_for :title, "Styleguide" %>

<div class="sg">
  <h1>üsgu styleguide</h1>
  <p class="sg-lede">
    Every specimen below is the real shared element, rendered with the app's own
    bundled CSS. Each entry names the <b>one purpose</b> its element telegraphs.
  </p>
  <p class="sg-lede">
    <b>Green is the dominant accent</b> &mdash; interaction (links, focus, primary),
    state (today, selected) and follows (the green star). <b>Raspberry is rare</b>:
    the saved-show heart alone. The two personal signals differ in colour AND shape,
    never colour alone. Structural rules use a neutral hairline
    (<code>--border-color</code>) or content divider (<code>--rule-color</code>).
  </p>

  <nav class="sg-toc">
    <a href="#colours">Colour intent</a>
    <a href="#buttons">Buttons &amp; actions</a>
    <a href="#pills">Pills, badges &amp; chips</a>
    <a href="#dropdowns">Dropdowns &amp; selects</a>
    <a href="#inputs">Form inputs</a>
    <a href="#genre-combobox">Genre picker</a>
    <a href="#drop-zone">Drop zone</a>
    <a href="#icons">Icons</a>
    <a href="#nav">Navigation</a>
    <a href="#catalogue-controls">Catalogue controls</a>
    <a href="#pagination">Pagination</a>
    <a href="#page-header">Page header</a>
    <a href="#text-pages">Text pages</a>
    <a href="#review-card">Review card</a>
    <a href="#footer">Footer</a>
  </nav>

  <section class="sg-section" id="colours">
    <h2>Colour intent</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">
      Each semantic token should carry exactly one meaning. Swatches read live
      from the theme tokens (toggle the theme to see dark values).
    </p>
    <ul class="sg-swatches">
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--accent"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Accent</b> · <code>--theme-accent-color</code><br>The dominant accent: interaction (links, focus, primary), state (today, selected), <b>and follows</b> (the green star + followed tags)</p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--accent-mut"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Accent muted</b> · <code>--theme-accent-muted</code><br>Quiet accent ground (window chips)</p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--on-accent"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>On accent</b> · <code>--theme-on-accent</code><br>Text and glyphs painted ON the accent fill (primary buttons, badges, today, ticks). Set to the page background for the "punched out" look.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--favorite"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Saved</b> · <code>--theme-saved-color</code><br>Raspberry — the saved-show heart only, never follows. One emphatic colour, used sparingly.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--warn"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Warn</b> · <code>--theme-warn-color</code><br>Destructive / error only</p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--amber"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Amber</b> · <code>--color-amber</code><br>Neutral "empty / nothing here" status</p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--community"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Community</b> · <code>--theme-community-color</code><br>Steel blue — provenance only: a human entered this event and no scraper re-derives it.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--bg"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Background</b> · <code>--theme-bg-color</code></p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--bg-mut"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Background muted</b> · <code>--theme-bg-muted</code><br>Neutral fills, and the sand wash behind a hovered or selected dropdown option</p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--fg"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Foreground</b> · <code>--theme-fg-color</code></p>
      </li>
      <li class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip sg-swatch__chip--fg-mut"></div>
        <p class="sg-swatch__label"><b>Foreground muted</b> · <code>--theme-fg-muted</code><br>Secondary text, at-rest chrome/icons</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="buttons">
    <h2>Buttons &amp; actions</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro"><b>Three weights:</b> primary → secondary → danger, plus the flat icon action and the text link. Weight is the role; size (full-width vs small pill) is context. <b>At most one filled button per page</b>, so it is the thing that stands out.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <input type="submit" value="Save">
        <button type="button" class="button-small primary">Done</button>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Primary</span> · <code>input[type=submit]</code> / <code>.primary</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The one main commit of a page — filled accent. <code>input[type=submit]</code> is primary automatically; a non-submit primary opts in with <code>.primary</code> at any size.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <button type="button" class="button">Enable</button>
        <button type="button" class="button-small">Test now</button>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Secondary</span> · <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> / <code>.button</code> / <code>.button-small</code> (default)
        <p class="sg-purpose">Every action that is neither primary nor destructive — hollow accent, full-size or pill.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <button type="button" class="button-small danger">Delete rule</button>
        <span class="account-form"><button type="button" class="button delete">Delete account</button></span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Danger</span> · <code>.button-small.danger</code> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <code>.button.delete</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A destructive, hard-to-undo action. Hollow warn at rest, fills warn on hover/focus.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <a href="#buttons" class="icon-button" aria-label="Edit"><span class="ph ph-gear"></span></a>
        <button type="button" class="icon-button danger" aria-label="Delete"><span class="ph ph-trash"></span></button>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Icon button</span> · <code>.icon-button</code>, <code>.icon-button.danger</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A flat, boxless inline icon action on a row (edit gear, delete trash). Muted at rest → foreground on hover; danger → warn on hover.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= form_with url: "#buttons", method: :get do |f| %>
          <%= render layout: "shared/form_actions", locals: { form: f, submit_label: "Speichern", cancel_path: "#buttons" } do %>
            <a href="#buttons" class="button-small danger">Löschen</a>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Form actions</span> · <code>render "shared/form_actions", form:, submit_label:, cancel_path:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The closing row of a task-style form: primary submit plus an explicit <b>Abbrechen</b> to <code>cancel_path</code>, so backing out never depends on scrolling up to the header. Extra actions ride in a block via <code>render layout:</code>; anything <code>.danger</code>/<code>.delete</code> is pushed to the far end. In-place forms (Settings) and entry gates with an alternate-path link take none.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen"><a href="#buttons" class="text-link">Open filter</a></div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Text link</span> · <code>.text-link</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Navigation rendered as an underlined accent link — borderless, because it is a link and not a control box.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen"><button type="button" class="theme-toggle" aria-label="Theme"><span class="ph ph-moon"></span></button></div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Theme toggle</span> · <code>.theme-toggle</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Icon-only accent button; toggles light ↔ dark.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="view-switcher inline-flex">
          <a href="#buttons" class="view-switch__item active"><b>Unread</b></a>
          <a href="#buttons" class="view-switch__item">Read</a>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">View switcher</span> · <code>.view-switch__item</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The shared flat text toggle between sibling views of one page (the inbox's Ungelesen ↔ Gelesen): active = bold accent, the rest muted underlined links. Flat-text controls use their own classes rather than borrowing <code>.button</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <input type="submit" value="Disabled" disabled>
        <button type="button" class="button-small" disabled>Disabled</button>
        <button type="button" class="button primary" disabled>Disabled primary</button>
        <button type="button" class="button-small primary" disabled>Disabled primary</button>
        <a href="#buttons" class="button-small">Focus me (Tab)</a>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">States</span> · <code>:disabled</code>, <code>:focus-visible</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Disabled is 0.5 opacity, a not-allowed cursor, and no fill — so a <b>primary</b> has to give up its <code>--theme-on-accent</code> text at the same time, or the label is left painted in the page background and the button reads as an empty box. Both primary weights are specimened for that reason. Tab to any control to see the shared focus ring.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="pills">
    <h2>Pills, badges &amp; chips</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro"><b>Governing rule: a box reads as clickable.</b> Buttons are the only bordered/filled boxes — so anything with a border or solid fill says "do something", and <b>information carries no border/fill</b> (a faint tint at most). That's how you tell a read-only channel pill from a ghost action button at a glance.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="chip">In-app</span>
        <span class="chip chip--window">Mon–Sun</span>
        <span class="chip chip--type">New events</span>
        <span class="chip chip--muted">Disabled</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Info chip</span> · <code>.chip</code> (<code>--window</code>, <code>--type</code>, <code>--muted</code>)
        <p class="sg-purpose">Read-only metadata that is never clickable (channels, windows, rule type, disabled state).</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:6px;">
          <span><span style="text-decoration: line-through underline;">Called-off show <span class="event-link-marker" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></span><span class="chip chip--cancelled">Cancelled</span></span>
          <span><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Moved show <span class="event-link-marker" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></span><span class="chip chip--moved">New date</span></span>
          <span><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Community show <span class="event-link-marker" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></span><span class="chip chip--community">Community</span><span class="chip chip--source">Instagram</span></span>
          <span><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Off-site show <span class="event-link-marker" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></span><span class="chip chip--source">Bewegungsmelder</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Event markers</span> · <code>.chip--cancelled</code>, <code>.chip--moved</code>, <code>.chip--community</code>, <code>.chip--source</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A quiet <code>.chip</code> sub-family trailing an event title, sized down so it never competes with the title. <b>Status</b> runs warm by severity: cancelled (warn-red, struck title) → rescheduled (sand). <b>Provenance</b> runs cool or neutral: <b>community</b> (steel blue) marks an event a contributor entered by hand, <b>source</b> (grey) names where a link leaves you and shows only on links that are not the venue's own page. The two are independent and regularly land on the same title, which is why they do not share a colour.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render "shared/suggestions", label: "Known towns:", chips: [
              { label: "Bern", attrs: {} }, { label: "Biel", attrs: {} },
              { label: "Thun", attrs: {} }] %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Suggestion row</span> · <code>shared/_suggestions</code> · <code>.suggestions</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Values the app already carries, offered under the field they fill, in a <a href="#inputs">field group</a>'s <code>attached</code> slot. The one place a <code>.chip</code> is clickable: tapping fills the field rather than stating a fact, and nothing ever auto-applies. A whole vocabulary has no ranking to render, so it stays out of the row until the contributor's own letters rank it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="badge">3</span>
        <span class="badge">+2 more</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Count badge</span> · <code>.badge</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A small accent count attached to something else (unread notifications, "+N more").</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="tag">Techno</span>
        <span class="tag active">Jazz</span>
        <button type="button" class="tag">Ambient</button>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Selectable tag</span> · <code>.tag</code>, <code>.tag.active</code>, <code>button.tag</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A style or query token. <code>.active</code> (filled accent) is the current selection. <b>No ×</b> — it is a state, not something removable; a trailing × is the tell that a chip removes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip">
          <span class="filter-chip__icon ph ph-music-notes"></span>
          <span class="filter-chip__label">Jazz</span>
          <span class="filter-chip__remove ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Applied filter chip</span> · <code>.filter-chip</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">An active filter on the mobile summary row; tapping it removes that one value. Dims on hover/focus to signal the affordance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="tag active" data-tag-chip><span class="ph ph-map-trifold" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>BE</span><span class="tag__remove ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
        <span class="tag active" data-tag-chip><span class="ph ph-map-pin" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Bern</span><span class="tag__remove ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
        <span class="tag active" data-tag-chip><span class="ph ph-house" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Dachstock</span><span class="tag__remove ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Applied location chip (desktop)</span> · <code>.tag[data-tag-chip]</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A removable location filter (inline desktop filter + rule editor). The leading icon is <b>per type</b> — canton <code>map-trifold</code> / locality <code>map-pin</code> / venue <code>house</code> — matching the dropdown and the mobile sheet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="scrape-badge scrape-badge--ok">OK</span>
        <span class="scrape-badge scrape-badge--empty">No results</span>
        <span class="scrape-badge scrape-badge--failed">2 failed</span>
        <span class="scrape-badge scrape-badge--running">Running</span>
        <span class="scrape-badge scrape-badge--snoozed">Snoozed</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Status badge</span> · <code>.scrape-badge--{ok,empty,failed,running,snoozed}</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Scrape outcome, encoded by hue (green/amber/red/grey). The one place a solid green pill means "success" rather than "primary/selected". Snoozed is grey — a deliberately skipped scraper, not a fault.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="dropdowns">
    <h2>Dropdowns &amp; selects</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">Specimens shown with the real account-form treatment.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="account-form">
          <select aria-label="Language">
            <option value="" selected>Choose a language…</option>
            <option>German</option><option>French</option><option>English</option>
          </select>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Styled select</span> · <code>.account-form select</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">An underline field with a chevron, matching the form fields. Neutral underline at rest, accent on focus.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <details class="nav-menu">
          <summary>account</summary>
          <div class="nav-menu__items">
            <a href="#nav">Settings</a>
            <a href="#nav">Log out</a>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Menu dropdown</span> · <code>.nav-menu</code> (<code>&lt;details&gt;</code>)
        <p class="sg-purpose">Collapses account links into a bordered panel; the summary is the trigger, carrying the shared Phosphor caret that rotates on open.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="inputs">
    <h2>Form inputs</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">Two field skins: underline (forms) and borderless-grow (filter bar).</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="account-form flex flex-col gap-small">
          <span class="field-label">Field label</span>
          <span class="muted">A short hint — muted and smaller.</span>
          <input type="text" placeholder="value / input" aria-label="Field">
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Field label / value / hint</span> · <code>.field-label</code> + <code>.muted</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">One typographic ladder per field, in reading order: a <b>bold</b> <code>.field-label</code> (a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> over a value/select, or a fieldset <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code>), then a muted, smaller <code>.muted</code> hint, then the normal-weight value — so the hint is read <em>before</em> you fill the field. Every label in a section uses this one style.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <div class="account-form flex flex-col gap-large">
          <%= render layout: "shared/field_group", locals: {
                attached: [render("shared/cite", quote: "3007 ZORPWIL"),
                           render("shared/suggestions", label: "Known towns:",
                                  chips: [{ label: "Zorpwil", attrs: {} },
                                          { label: "Flarnhausen", attrs: {} }])] } do %>
            <div class="flex gap-small wrap">
              <label class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall flex-grow">
                <span class="field-label">Ortschaft</span>
                <input type="text" value="Zorpwil">
              </label>
              <label class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall flex-grow">
                <span class="field-label">Kanton</span>
                <select><option>Bern</option></select>
              </label>
            </div>
          <% end %>
          <%= render layout: "shared/field_group", locals: {
                attached: tag.span("Enter adds one.", class: "muted") } do %>
            <label class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall">
              <span class="field-label">Genres</span>
              <input type="text" value="Zorpcore, Flarnwave">
            </label>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Field group</span> · <code>render layout: "shared/field_group", attached:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A field — or a pair of fields settled from <b>one source</b>, as Ortschaft and Kanton are here — plus what hangs off it: <code>attached</code> takes the lines under it (a <code>cite</code>, a suggestion row, a hint) as one renderable or a list, blanks dropping out. No rule, box, tint or indent: the lines inside a group sit at <code>gap-xsmall</code> while the column holding the groups gaps at <code>gap-large</code>, and that difference is the only thing saying which field a line belongs to — a caller that gaps its column tighter has no grouping left. Attach to the pair wherever both fields come from that one source.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="account-form flex flex-col gap-medium">
          <textarea rows="3" placeholder="Paste text here" aria-label="Text"></textarea>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Multi-line field</span> · <code>.account-form textarea</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The same underline skin on a textarea. It resizes vertically only — sideways resizing breaks the form column.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <div class="account-form">
          <div class="flex gap-small wrap">
            <label class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall flex-grow">
              <span class="field-label">Datum</span>
              <input type="date" value="2026-09-01">
            </label>
            <label class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall flex-grow">
              <span class="field-label">Zeit</span>
              <%= render "shared/time_field", name: :styleguide_time, value: "20:00" %>
            </label>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Date + time pair</span> · <code>.account-form input[type=date]</code> + <code>render "shared/time_field", name:, value:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose"><b>Both halves are native pickers</b> — never pair one with a plain text field. A date/time control takes its height from the value box the engine lays out in its shadow DOM, and mobile Safari holds on to its own control metrics whatever height the stylesheet sets, so a text field beside it draws its underline somewhere else. <b>Check this specimen on a real iPhone</b>: a desktop browser lines a date up with a text field either way.</p>
        <p class="sg-purpose"><b>Use the time partial rather than a bare <code>input[type=time]</code></b>, wherever a time may be unknown. It adds the ✕ that clears the field — no engine ships one, and iOS Safari's wheel picker has no empty position to scroll back to — so an event with no printed start time can be entered as having none. The ✕ shows only once the field holds a value, and it overlays the control's right end so the pair still spans its row.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="account-form flex gap-medium wrap">
          <input type="text" placeholder="Username" aria-label="Username">
          <input type="password" placeholder="Password" aria-label="Password">
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Account / auth field</span> · <code>.account-form input</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Underline-only field: neutral bottom border, accent on focus, foreground text.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <label class="inline-flex gap-small align-center">
          <input type="checkbox" checked> Native checkbox
        </label>
        <label class="tag">
          <input type="checkbox" checked> Chip checkbox
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Checkboxes</span> · <code>input[type=checkbox]</code> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <code>label.tag</code> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <code>.opt__box</code> (sheets)
        <p class="sg-purpose">Confirm an opt-in. One custom box (left) everywhere; the selectable chip fills accent when checked.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <div style="min-width: 12rem; border: var(--border-width) solid var(--rule-color);">
          <label class="opt"><input type="checkbox"><span class="opt__box"></span><span class="opt__label">Multi (checkbox)</span></label>
          <label class="opt opt--single"><input type="checkbox" checked><span class="opt__box"></span><span class="opt__label">Single (radio)</span></label>
          <label class="opt opt--single"><input type="checkbox"><span class="opt__box"></span><span class="opt__label">Single, unpicked</span></label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Sheet option rows</span> · <code>.opt</code> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <code>.opt--single</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The checkable rows inside a filter sheet (What / Where / When). The box shape is the only signal: square is multi-select, <code>.opt--single</code> rounds it to a radio dot for a sheet that takes exactly one value.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <div style="min-width: 12rem; border: var(--border-width) solid var(--rule-color);">
          <p class="sheet__loading"><%= t('events.filter.loading') %></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Sheet loading row</span> · <code>.sheet__loading</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Stands in for a sheet's option rows while they load — the What and Where trees run to a few hundred rows, so they are fetched the first time the sheet opens. Muted, one line, and it reserves a few rows' height so the in-flow desktop panel does not jump when the tree lands.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="genre-combobox">
    <h2>Genre picker</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">The one field for choosing an event's genres, wherever that happens: the capture card, the hand-entry page, the admin event editor. Built from <code>shared/_genre_combobox</code> &mdash; <b>reuse it</b> rather than configuring a combobox by hand, because three of its options are load-bearing and silently break the field if they drift apart.</p>
    <p class="sg-section__intro"><b>Free text, and therefore names.</b> A poster names genres the taxonomy has never seen, so typing a new one is expected, and the gem submits a newly-typed genre under the same field name as the picked ones &mdash; which is why every option is keyed by its <b>name</b> and not by a <code>Genre</code> id. <code>mobile_at: "0px"</code> keeps the listbox inline at every width: the gem's modal <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> covers a phone from the middle down and then loses its lower half to the software keyboard.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <div class="account-form flex flex-col gap-small">
          <%= render "shared/genre_combobox", name: :styleguide_genres, id: "sg-genres",
                value: "", chip_src: chips_genres_path, label: t('capture.candidate.genres'),
                options: genre_combobox_options(Genre.offerable) %>
          <span class="muted"><%= t('capture.candidate.genres_hint') %></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Genre picker</span> &middot; <code>render "shared/genre_combobox", name:, id:, value:, chip_src:, label:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Each option reads <b>name &middot; where it sits</b> on the left and a descendant count on the right, umbrella genres sorted to the top. Both are render-only: typing still filters on the name alone.</p>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Pass <code>badge:</code> to hang a chip off the label, and <code>options: []</code> to render an empty listbox for a client that clones the page's one copy into it. The label carries <code>for</code> and must <b>never</b> wrap the field: a tap on a selection chip inside a wrapping label is forwarded to the input as a second click, defeating the chip's own remover.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="drop-zone">
    <h2>Drop zone</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">A file picker drawn as a drop target: drop files on it, tap it to open the system picker, or paste an image onto it. It holds nothing and lists nothing &mdash; what happens on pick belongs to the caller.</p>

    <div class="sg-row sg-row--stack">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render "shared/drop_zone", id: "sg-drop-zone",
              label: t('capture.picker.drop_label'), hint: t('capture.images_hint') %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Drop zone</span> · <code>render "shared/drop_zone", id:, label:, hint:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A real <code>&lt;input type="file"&gt;</code> stays behind the dashed target, visually hidden and wrapped by a <code>&lt;label for&gt;</code>: the drop handler is an <b>enhancement</b>, and without the input keyboard users and every iOS browser lose the picker entirely. The dashed edge is the only one on the site, so a drop target is never mistaken for a field. Pass <code>zone_attrs</code>/<code>input_attrs</code> for the caller's own hooks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row sg-row--stack">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render "shared/drop_zone", id: "sg-drop-zone-paste",
              label: t('capture.picker.drop_label'), hint: t('capture.images_hint'),
              paste_label: t('capture.picker.paste'), paste_error: t('capture.picker.paste_empty'),
              error_attrs: { hidden: false } %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">…with a paste button</span> · <code>paste_label:</code>, <code>paste_error:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A third way in for a phone, which has no keystroke for pasting. The button is a <b>sibling</b> of the <code>&lt;label for&gt;</code> and never inside it — a label forwards every tap in its subtree to the file input, which would open the system picker instead. The caller hides it where <code>navigator.clipboard.read</code> is missing. The refusal is specimened here; live it starts hidden.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="icons">
    <h2>Icons</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">Phosphor Regular (base class <code>ph</code>); the follow <b>star</b> and saved <b>heart</b> are masked SVGs (outline→fill for off/on). Clickable icons use <code>.icon-button</code>, display-only icons the <code>.icon</code> role.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen sg-specimen--lg">
        <span class="icon ph ph-calendar-dots"></span>
        <span class="icon ph ph-map-pin"></span>
        <span class="filter-icon ph ph-magnifying-glass"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Display icon</span> · <code>.icon</code> (muted) · <code>.filter-icon</code> (green)
        <p class="sg-purpose">A non-interactive metadata glyph is muted (<code>.icon</code>, the counterpart to the clickable <code>.icon-button</code>). <b>Exception:</b> a filter field's leading handle (<code>.filter-icon</code> / <code>.filter-trigger__icon</code>) is accent-green — the field opens a dropdown, so the glyph reads as an interactive affordance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen sg-specimen--lg">
        <span class="ph ph-gear" title="ph-gear"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-trash" title="ph-trash"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-bell" title="ph-bell"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-x" title="ph-x"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-magnifying-glass" title="ph-magnifying-glass"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-caret-down" title="ph-caret-down"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-map-pin" title="ph-map-pin"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-house" title="ph-house"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-map-trifold" title="ph-map-trifold"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-music-notes" title="ph-music-notes"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-tag" title="ph-tag"></span>
        <span class="ph ph-calendar-dots" title="ph-calendar-dots"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Glyph set</span> · <code>.ph .ph-*</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Hover a glyph to see its name. Edit, delete, notify, close/remove, search, disclosure, locality/venue/canton, style/genre, date. (Follow/save use the masked star/heart below, not a font glyph.)</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="filter-menu__toggle"><span class="ph ph-funnel" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
        <span class="filter-menu__toggle"><span class="funnel-fill" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
        <span class="save-filter-icon"><span class="ph ph-funnel" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="save-filter-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Saved-filters menu</span> · <code>.filter-menu</code>, <code>.funnel-fill</code>, <code>.save-filter-icon</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The saved-filter control beside the applied-filter chips: a funnel <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> menu that <b>saves</b> the active filter and <b>applies</b> a saved one. Outline funnel = nothing saved here; solid <b>green</b> funnel = the active filter is itself saved. Inside, the <b>+</b> badge marks the save item.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen sg-specimen--lg">
        <button type="button" class="event-save icon-button" aria-label="Save"><span class="save-heart"></span></button>
        <button type="button" class="event-save icon-button saved" aria-label="Saved"><span class="save-heart"></span></button>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Save heart</span> · <code>.save-heart</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">"Save this show" — the rare, powerful signal, and the one raspberry on the site. Faint outline = not saved, solid <b>raspberry</b> = saved. Its counterpart is the green <b>star</b> of a saved filter: the two personal signals differ in shape as well as colour.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="nav">
    <h2>Navigation</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">Header/footer chrome and the responsive filter (inline ≥600px, full-screen sheets &lt;600px) are composed from the elements above; the live versions surround this page.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="view-switcher inline-flex">
          <a href="#nav" class="view-switch__item active"><b>Unread</b></a>
          <a href="#nav" class="view-switch__item">Read</a>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">View switcher</span> · <code>.view-switcher</code> / <code>.view-switch__item</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Flat text toggle between sibling views of one page; active = bold accent.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <span class="unread-dot" role="img" aria-label="Unread"></span>
        <span>username</span>
        <span class="badge">3</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Unread signal</span> · <code>.unread-dot</code> + <code>.badge</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A dot on the menu trigger flags unread at a glance; the count badge sits beside the Notifications item inside the menu.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="catalogue-controls">
    <h2>Catalogue controls</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">Every catalogue browser — admin events / localities / locations / places, and the genre index — opens with the same three blocks in the same order: <b>filter chips</b>, then the <b>search field</b>, then the <b>sort row</b>. Built from <code>shared/_catalogue_controls</code>; pass the route helper as a symbol, the i18n scope, and the two lists. <b>Reuse it</b> rather than hand-rolling the row.</p>
    <p class="sg-section__intro"><b>The three blocks are one component because each has to carry the other two&rsquo;s params.</b> A chip that drops <code>sort</code> silently resets the ordering every time you filter; a sort link that drops the filter throws you back to the full list. The partial builds all three URLs from one place.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render "shared/catalogue_controls", route: :admin_events_path, scope: "admin.events.index",
              filters: %w[all visible hidden cancelled], active_filter: "all",
              sorts: %w[date title], active_sort: "date" %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Catalogue controls</span> &middot; <code>render "shared/catalogue_controls", route:, scope:, filters:, active_filter:, sorts:, active_sort:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The active chip fills accent (<code>.tag.active</code>); the active sort option goes full-colour and bold while the rest stay muted, and neither reads as an underlined link. The sort row&rsquo;s label is one shared key (<code>catalogue.sort_by</code>) for every page. <code>filters</code> leads with <code>"all"</code>, which maps to <b>no</b> filter param rather than the literal string, so the unfiltered URL stays clean.</p>
        <p class="sg-purpose"><code>filter_param:</code> names the query param <em>and</em> the i18n key prefix at once — the locations browser passes <code>:type</code> and gets <code>type_venue</code> keys with a <code>?type=</code> URL. <code>divider_before:</code> names the chip that opens a second group, which is how the genre index files its parked dispositions apart from its tree statuses.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="pagination">
    <h2>Pagination</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">Every long list closes with the same quiet pager: prev/next plus a <code>Seite X / Y</code> readout, <b>never</b> a number grid, so it stays one calm line at any width. Built from <code>shared/_pagination</code>; pass the Kaminari <code>collection</code>. It renders nothing for a single page, and the end you cannot move past shows as muted, inert text so the readout never shifts as you page.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render 'shared/pagination', collection: Kaminari.paginate_array((1..150).to_a).page(2).per(50) %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Pager</span> · <code>render 'shared/pagination', collection: @events</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Use it everywhere a <code>.page(params[:page])</code> collection is listed, so the pager reads identically across admin and app.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="page-header">
    <h2>Page header &amp; back link</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">Every page except the events feed opens with the same block: an optional <b>back link</b> — the "up" navigation — above the title. Built from <code>shared/_page_header</code> + <code>shared/_back_link</code>; <b>reuse them</b> rather than hand-rolling a header. The ← is decorative and lives in the partial, never in the copy.</p>
    <p class="sg-section__intro"><b>The rule:</b> the back link points <b>up one level</b>, and the top of the tree is the events feed. A detail or edit page links to its parent list; a top-level page reached from the nav links back to the feed (<code>root_path</code>, label <code>nav.events</code>). Only the feed itself and the pre-login auth pages omit it.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render layout: "shared/page_header", locals: { back_path: "#page-header", back_label: "All saved filters" } do %>
          <h1>Page title <span class="muted">12</span></h1>
          <p class="muted">A muted subtitle / meta line.</p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Page header</span> · <code>render layout: "shared/page_header"</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Put the <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> (plus any kicker, count, meta or inline action) in the block; pass <code>back_path</code> / <code>back_label</code> for the up-link, or omit them on a top-level page. Renders as the first child of the page's <code>flex flex-col gap-large</code> column.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="text-pages">
    <h2>Text pages</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">The two long-form pages — <b>Über üsgu</b> and <b>Datenschutz</b>. Prose, not chrome: a <code>.text-page</code> column narrowed to a readable measure, holding one <code>.prose</code> block of plain ERB. <b>Both pages have the same shape</b>, so the tiers below are the whole vocabulary; a third text page copies it rather than inventing a variant.</p>
    <p class="sg-section__intro"><b>Every heading is a direct child of <code>.prose</code></b> — no <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> wrappers. The section break is a top margin on the heading itself, which a wrapper would put out of reach; nothing is gained in exchange, because no browser or screen reader implements the sectioning outline.</p>

    <div class="sg-row sg-row--stack">
      <div class="sg-specimen sg-specimen--block">
        <div class="text-page">
          <div class="prose flex flex-col gap-medium">
            <p>The intro paragraph, unheaded, sitting directly under the page title.</p>
            <h2>A section heading</h2>
            <p>Body copy. Space Mono has no width variation and a very even stroke density, so <code>.prose</code> carries more leading than chrome text to keep the lines apart.</p>
            <h3>A subhead</h3>
            <p>The h3 tier is a spaced uppercase label, not a bigger bold sentence — at base size, bold alone is too weak a signal in a monospace face. It reads as a subhead by shape, so it never competes with <a href="#text-pages">an inline link</a>.</p>
            <h2>A section with a list</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Bulleted items sit tighter to each other than paragraphs do.</li>
              <li>They take the section break from the heading above them.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Prose block</span> · <code>.text-page &gt; .prose.flex.flex-col.gap-medium</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Four tiers only: <code>h2</code> section, <code>h3</code> subhead, paragraph, list. <b>Spacing is what separates sections</b> — the flex gap gives every child the same 10px, so <code>h2</code> and <code>h3</code> add a top margin to buy the break, and the ratio above vs. below a heading is what groups it with its own copy. Inline links are underlined here and nowhere else in the app: chrome links read as links from position and colour, a link mid-sentence does not.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="review-card">
    <h2>Review card</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">One thing being judged, with the evidence that settles it. An ordinary block in document flow: the source at the top (left of the fields from 900px), the fields below it, the decision after the last field, and <b>one</b> page scroll for the whole card. Nothing in it holds still — a pane that stayed put while the page moved could only do it by letting the fields pass behind it. The source is capped so the first field is on screen beside it, and each field carries the line quoted off the source, so the comparison survives scrolling past the poster.</p>

    <div class="sg-row sg-row--stack">
      <div class="sg-specimen sg-specimen--block">
        <%= render layout: "shared/review_card",
              locals: { id: "sg-review-card", source: image_tag("/icon.png", alt: ""),
                        actions: render(layout: "shared/action_bar") {
                          safe_join([tag.button("Veröffentlichen", class: "button-small primary", type: "button"),
                                     tag.button("Verwerfen", class: "button-small", type: "button")])
                        } } do %>
          <p class="field-label">poster.png</p>
          <div class="account-form flex flex-col gap-large">
            <label class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall">
              <span class="field-label">Titel</span>
              <input type="text" value="Zorpcore Nacht">
            </label>
            <%= render layout: "shared/field_group",
                  locals: { attached: render("shared/cite", quote: "3007 ZORPWIL") } do %>
              <label class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall">
                <span class="field-label">Ortschaft</span>
                <input type="text" value="Zorpwil">
              </label>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Review card</span> · <code>render layout: "shared/review_card", id:, actions:, source:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The block is the body. <code>actions</code> is a pre-rendered local rather than a second block so the decision row cannot be written into the middle of the field list; <code>source</code> is the evidence, or is left out and written into the pane by a client that holds it in memory only. Pass <code>frame_class</code>/<code>frame_attrs</code> for the caller's own hooks — never a second <code>class</code> attribute.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <div class="account-form flex flex-col gap-large">
          <%= render layout: "shared/field_group",
                locals: { attached: render("shared/cite", quote: "3007 ZORPWIL") } do %>
            <label class="flex flex-col gap-xsmall">
              <span class="field-label">Ortschaft</span>
              <input type="text" value="Zorpwil">
            </label>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Cite</span> · <code>render "shared/cite", quote:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The verbatim text a model quoted as its source for the field <b>above</b> it — provenance for a value already filled in, which is why it reads after the field rather than before it like a hint. Goes in a <a href="#inputs">field group</a>'s <code>attached</code> slot. It shares the muted channel with a hint and is set apart by <b>slant</b>: italic is the transcribed line, upright the instruction. Quotation marks come from the locale (<code>„…“</code> / <code>“…”</code> / <code>«&nbsp;…&nbsp;»</code>) and carry the whole meaning, so there is no repeated label. A blank <code>quote</code> renders nothing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row sg-row--stack">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render layout: "shared/card_aside",
              locals: { title: "Falsch? Markier, was nochmal ausgelesen werden soll:",
                        action: tag.button("Nochmal auslesen", type: "button", class: "button-small") } do %>
          <div class="account-form flex flex-col gap-small">
            <div class="flex gap-xsmall wrap">
              <label class="tag"><input type="checkbox"> Datum</label>
              <label class="tag"><input type="checkbox"> Lokal</label>
            </div>
            <input type="text" placeholder="Was steht da wirklich?">
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Card aside</span> · <code>render layout: "shared/card_aside", title:, action:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">A block inside a review card that is <b>not</b> part of what the card is deciding — a report on the read, a note, anything that does not post with the card's form. It separates itself by <b>kind</b> rather than weight: the card body is borderless, so every input already draws a horizontal rule and one more hairline reads as one more field, while a recessed ground and a heading read as a boundary. <code>action</code> stays beside its own controls rather than going down to the <a href="#review-card">action bar</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row sg-row--stack">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render "captures/matches", form_id: "sg-no-form",
              matches: [{ id: 1, title: "Zorpcore Nacht", meta: "21:00 · Zorpsaal",
                          adds: t('capture.matches.adds',
                                  fields: [t('capture.matches.fields.description'),
                                           t('capture.matches.fields.genres', count: 2)].join(", ")) },
                        { id: 2, title: "Zorpcore Nacht — Afterparty", meta: "23:00 · Zorpsaal",
                          adds: t('capture.matches.nothing') }] %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Match block</span> · <code>render "captures/matches", matches:, form_id:</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Shows we may already carry, at the <b>top</b> of a capture card because they ask about the whole card rather than one field. It is the one block in the body that is neither a field nor a <a href="#review-card">card aside</a>: it posts with the card's form but is not something to fill in, so it takes the recessed ground plus the amber <a href="#colours">attention</a> edge. Each row names what this read would <b>add</b> to that show. Every button is a submitter carrying its own <code>name</code>/<code>value</code> into the card's form by id, which is how one form posts three different answers with no client code.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render layout: "shared/action_bar" do %>
          <button type="button" class="button-small primary">Veröffentlichen</button>
          <button type="button" class="button-small">Verwerfen</button>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Action bar</span> · <code>render layout: "shared/action_bar"</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">The decision row of a review card, sitting after the last field where the form ends. It holds only the decisions that <b>end</b> the card: the commit first (primary), the quiet way out <b>last</b> — a dismissal next to the commit is one mis-tap away from being it. A control that leaves the card in play goes in a <a href="#review-card">card aside</a> instead. There is no <b>Abbrechen</b>: leaving decides nothing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-section" id="footer">
    <h2>Footer</h2>
    <p class="sg-section__intro">A quiet, in-flow row of secondary links (about + the privacy notice), rendered once at the bottom of every page by the layout. Deliberately <b>recessive</b> — small, foreground-muted text — so it never competes with the feed; it sits below <code>&lt;main&gt;</code> and pins to the bottom on short pages.</p>

    <div class="sg-row">
      <div class="sg-specimen">
        <%= render 'shared/footer' %>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-spec">
        <span class="sg-spec__name">Site footer</span> · <code>render 'shared/footer'</code>
        <p class="sg-purpose">Already in the application layout — pages do not render it themselves. Add a link here (and a route) only for a genuinely new low-priority or legal destination; keep the row scannable.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
